1
00:00:08,170 --> 00:00:09,500
- Hey.      - Hey.

2
00:00:10,630 --> 00:00:13,920
- What are you guys doing up?     - We wanted to finish the crossword before bed.

3
00:00:15,010 --> 00:00:17,760
Do you know a six-letter word for "red"?

4
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:20,100
Dark-red.

5
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,770
I think that's wrong, but there's a connect-the-dots in here for you later.

6
00:00:27,230 --> 00:00:29,110
Hey, how, uh, about maroon?

7
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:32,860
- Yes! You are so smart!     - Ha-ha-ha.

8
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:34,400
Aw.

9
00:00:34,570 --> 00:00:36,070
You guys are so cute.

10
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:37,950
I know.

11
00:00:38,490 --> 00:00:40,200
All right. I'll see you in the morning.

12
00:00:40,370 --> 00:00:41,990
Okay.

13
00:00:54,260 --> 00:00:57,130
You know, I love doing crossword puzzles with you, honey.

14
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:58,340
Oh, me too.

15
00:00:58,510 --> 00:01:00,970
- Now, let's finish this and go to bed.     - Okay.

16
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:02,600
There's only one left.

17
00:01:02,770 --> 00:01:06,270
Three-letter word. Not dog, but...

18
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:09,150
Cat.

19
00:01:10,190 --> 00:01:11,730
Yes. Ha.

20
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:14,030
You are so smart!

21
00:01:16,070 --> 00:01:17,240
I love you.

22
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:18,910
I love you too.

23
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:24,140
Uh.

24
00:02:24,350 --> 00:02:25,720
We still need a tip.

25
00:02:25,890 --> 00:02:28,430
All right. Hold on.

26
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:30,390
I got it.

27
00:02:30,770 --> 00:02:32,690
Nickel.

28
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:35,440
- How much more do we need?     - Couple of bucks.

29
00:02:36,030 --> 00:02:37,570
Okay, dime.

30
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:41,030
You guys should probably keep talking. This could take a while.

31
00:02:41,610 --> 00:02:42,870
Wait, lookit!

32
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:44,410
Whoa!

33
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:46,450
Oh, my God. This is a police badge!

34
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:50,960
Oh, cool. But why would a cop come in here? They don't serve doughnuts. Ha.

35
00:02:52,830 --> 00:02:54,250
Can you discover the badge again?

36
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:56,880
I think I can come up with something better than that.

37
00:02:58,130 --> 00:03:00,340
I bet somebody's missing that badge.

38
00:03:00,510 --> 00:03:03,640
I should take it back. Ooh, but while I'm at the police station...

39
00:03:03,890 --> 00:03:05,800
...I could check their Ten Most Wanted list.

40
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:09,930
My friend Fritzi's been Number 11 forever. This could be her year!

41
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:14,560
- Hey, you guys.     - Hey, Joey.

42
00:03:14,730 --> 00:03:17,070
- Hey.     - Hey.

43
00:03:17,230 --> 00:03:19,650
Is that my sweatshirt?

44
00:03:19,820 --> 00:03:23,280
Yes, it is. I'm sorry. I borrowed it. I was cold. I hope it's okay.

45
00:03:23,450 --> 00:03:26,910
It's just that, uh, if you wear someone's sweatshirt...

46
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:29,410
...shouldn't it be your boyfriend's?

47
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:31,250
And I'm not him.

48
00:03:32,710 --> 00:03:34,040
I'm sorry. I'll give it back.

49
00:03:34,210 --> 00:03:35,460
No, no. No.

50
00:03:35,630 --> 00:03:38,250
It's going to be all smelling like Monica.

51
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:40,300
Are you saying I smell bad?

52
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:41,510
No.

53
00:03:41,670 --> 00:03:43,930
You smell like a meadow.

54
00:03:46,180 --> 00:03:47,220
I'm sorry.

55
00:03:50,430 --> 00:03:51,480
What's with him?

56
00:03:51,730 --> 00:03:56,060
The last time Joey went to a meadow, his mother was shot by a hunter.

57
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:15,750
I still don't know.

58
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:19,880
I'm sorry, I just want to make sure I bought the right couch, one that says:

59
00:04:20,050 --> 00:04:24,380
"Kids welcome here," but that also says

60
00:04:24,630 --> 00:04:26,890
"Come here to me."

61
00:04:29,010 --> 00:04:32,600
What? You say that to kids?

62
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:34,060
No, no, no.

63
00:04:34,230 --> 00:04:38,730
The "Come here to me" is, you know, for the ladies.

64
00:04:39,610 --> 00:04:42,730
Ross, honey, it's a nice couch, not a magic couch.

65
00:04:44,570 --> 00:04:46,070
Well, you picked a great couch.

66
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:47,320
- Yeah?     - Yeah.

67
00:04:47,490 --> 00:04:48,990
- Sign here please.     - Sure.

68
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:51,450
Oh, what's, heh...?

69
00:04:51,620 --> 00:04:54,080
The delivery charge is almost as much as the couch!

70
00:04:54,330 --> 00:04:57,210
That's ridiculous. He lives three blocks away.

71
00:04:57,380 --> 00:05:00,420
You know what? I'll take it myself. Thank you.

72
00:05:01,090 --> 00:05:02,750
All right, Rach, come on. Let's go.

73
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:04,300
Yeah.

74
00:05:09,390 --> 00:05:11,260
Are you kidding?

75
00:05:12,060 --> 00:05:16,230
Come on. It's only three blocks. Uh, it's not very heavy. Try it.

76
00:05:21,570 --> 00:05:23,650
- Oh, I can do it.     - Yeah.

77
00:05:23,820 --> 00:05:26,490
You two will really enjoy that couch.

78
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:29,410
We're, uh, not together.

79
00:05:29,660 --> 00:05:31,450
Oh, okay. Yeah. Ha-ha-ha.

80
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:33,410
Something didn't quite add up there.

81
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:40,210
Ross.

82
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:42,170
- What's that supposed to mean?     - Ross.

83
00:05:42,340 --> 00:05:45,460
Well, you. Her. Heh.

84
00:05:45,670 --> 00:05:47,470
I mean, she's very...

85
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:48,930
...you know.

86
00:05:49,180 --> 00:05:50,800
And you're, like...

87
00:05:50,970 --> 00:05:52,800
...you know?

88
00:05:55,350 --> 00:05:59,190
Not that it's any of your business, but we did go out.

89
00:05:59,350 --> 00:06:00,650
Really? You two?

90
00:06:00,810 --> 00:06:01,860
Yeah. Rach?

91
00:06:02,020 --> 00:06:05,570
I don't want to do this now. I'm carrying a heavy couch.

92
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:08,070
Then tell him quickly.

93
00:06:08,650 --> 00:06:10,530
Fine. We went out.

94
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:12,990
Not only did we go out...

95
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:16,120
...we did it 298 times!

96
00:06:16,290 --> 00:06:18,000
Ross.

97
00:06:18,620 --> 00:06:20,040
Oh, my...

98
00:06:20,210 --> 00:06:24,090
Ugh, you kept count? You are such a loser!

99
00:06:25,170 --> 00:06:29,090
A loser you did it with 298 times!

100
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:35,430
Oh. Oh!

101
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:39,940
Excuse me, ma'am. You can't put your cigarette out on a tree.

102
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:41,810
Yeah, I can. It worked well.

103
00:06:42,650 --> 00:06:45,730
But you shouldn't. So don't ever do that again.

104
00:06:45,940 --> 00:06:48,860
I won't till I have my next cigarette.

105
00:06:49,110 --> 00:06:50,320
Hold it!

106
00:06:50,570 --> 00:06:52,490
NYPD. Freeze, punk!

107
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:54,120
What?

108
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:57,910
That's right. You are so busted.

109
00:06:58,080 --> 00:06:59,330
Book them.

110
00:07:01,170 --> 00:07:04,080
- Who are you talking to?     - Save it, red!

111
00:07:04,460 --> 00:07:08,380
Unless you want to spend the night in the slammer, you apologize to the tree.

112
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:11,430
I am not going to apologize to a tree.

113
00:07:12,010 --> 00:07:15,640
You apologize to the tree right now, or I am calling for backup.

114
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:19,310
Backup! Backup!

115
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:21,180
I'm sorry! Sorry!

116
00:07:21,390 --> 00:07:24,520
Okay, cancel backup! Cancel backup!

117
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:27,480
Okay.

118
00:07:27,650 --> 00:07:30,570
Didn't you say there was, um, an elevator in here?

119
00:07:30,740 --> 00:07:34,110
Uh, yes, I did, but there isn't. Here we go!

120
00:07:35,410 --> 00:07:37,200
Okay, go left.

121
00:07:37,370 --> 00:07:39,540
Left. Left.

122
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:43,120
Okay, you know what? There's no more left left.

123
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:46,040
Lift it straight up over your head.

124
00:07:46,210 --> 00:07:48,590
Straight up over your head. You can do it!

125
00:07:48,750 --> 00:07:50,010
You can do it!

126
00:07:50,170 --> 00:07:52,170
- Okay. You got it?     - Yeah.

127
00:07:52,340 --> 00:07:53,680
- Go, go.     - Good, good.

128
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:56,010
You got it, right? You got it, right? You got...

129
00:08:01,770 --> 00:08:04,810
Any chance you think the couch looks good there?

130
00:08:06,230 --> 00:08:07,610
This guy was all...

131
00:08:08,980 --> 00:08:10,900
And I'm all, "Buffay! Homicide!"

132
00:08:12,610 --> 00:08:14,400
It was just so cool! Ha-ha-ha.

133
00:08:14,860 --> 00:08:16,870
Phoebe, you were supposed to take that back.

134
00:08:17,070 --> 00:08:19,410
I know, but I'm having so much fun doing good deeds.

135
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:23,540
Okay, but impersonating a police officer is a serious thing. You can get arrested.

136
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:26,250
You could get arrested right now!

137
00:08:29,250 --> 00:08:32,760
All right, yeah, I'd better take it back. I'm totally drunk with power.

138
00:08:36,390 --> 00:08:38,430
- Hey.     - Hey.

139
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:40,640
Oh.

140
00:08:41,970 --> 00:08:43,390
Hi, Joe.

141
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:46,270
Yeah. I didn't know you guys were gonna be here.

142
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:49,060
- Do me a favor, sweetie. Taste this.     - What? Why?

143
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:52,030
- What is going on with you?     - Nothing.

144
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:53,940
You've been acting strange all day.

145
00:08:54,570 --> 00:08:57,610
All right. There is something. I, uh...

146
00:08:58,410 --> 00:09:00,740
I kind of had a dream.

147
00:09:01,660 --> 00:09:03,870
But I don't want to talk about it.

148
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:07,000
Oh, whoa. What if Martin Luther King had said that?

149
00:09:08,710 --> 00:09:11,250
I kind of have a dream.

150
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:14,380
I don't want to talk about it.

151
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:18,390
Look, it involved Monica.

152
00:09:18,550 --> 00:09:21,430
You had a dream about a girl I'm seeing? Oh, that is so cool.

153
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:23,890
I can't tell you how many times I dreamt about a girl he was seeing.

154
00:09:24,060 --> 00:09:27,730
Anyway, we were talking about your dream. I love you. Your dream?

155
00:09:28,060 --> 00:09:31,400
Don't worry, there wasn't any sex in it. I haven't dreamt about her like that...

156
00:09:31,610 --> 00:09:34,190
...since I found out about you two-ish.

157
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,450
What was the dream about?

158
00:09:40,620 --> 00:09:42,950
Well, okay.

159
00:09:43,410 --> 00:09:47,040
You were my girlfriend. We were doing the crossword puzzle.

160
00:09:47,290 --> 00:09:49,080
Like you guys were doing last night.

161
00:09:49,330 --> 00:09:52,460
So that's it. I'm in love with Monica and I'll be moving out.

162
00:09:52,630 --> 00:09:56,420
Joey, come on. That doesn't mean that you're in love with me.

163
00:09:57,090 --> 00:09:58,130
It doesn't?

164
00:09:58,300 --> 00:10:00,140
It could mean anything. Like, uh...

165
00:10:00,390 --> 00:10:03,760
...all of a sudden you're jealous that I've become the apartment stud.

166
00:10:04,770 --> 00:10:06,470
Kind of sounds like your dream, dude.

167
00:10:09,190 --> 00:10:13,610
Or it could mean you saw Chandler and me together, being close and stuff...

168
00:10:13,770 --> 00:10:16,150
...and you just wanna have that with someone too.

169
00:10:16,570 --> 00:10:18,780
In the dream I did enjoy the closeness.

170
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:20,450
Okay, look.

171
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:21,950
Are you attracted to Monica?

172
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:24,410
Right here, right now, are you attracted to her?

173
00:10:27,790 --> 00:10:29,830
- Not really.     - There you have it!

174
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:33,460
Heh. Well, sure! I'm just wearing sweats!

175
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:36,050
But that's good!

176
00:10:36,210 --> 00:10:39,380
You're not in love with me. You just want a girlfriend.

177
00:10:39,550 --> 00:10:42,090
No, I don't think it's just about getting a girlfriend.

178
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:43,720
Yeah, I could get a girlfriend.

179
00:10:43,890 --> 00:10:47,060
Yeah, we could sit in the chair and do crossword puzzles.

180
00:10:47,220 --> 00:10:50,100
But are we ever gonna have the closeness like you guys have?

181
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:54,610
Monica and I were friends before we started dating. Maybe that's it.

182
00:10:54,770 --> 00:10:56,690
Friends first?

183
00:10:56,900 --> 00:10:58,570
That's interesting.

184
00:10:59,610 --> 00:11:03,370
- You become friends after?     - No, never done that either.

185
00:11:04,620 --> 00:11:06,910
Um, do you guys have a tape measure?

186
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:08,830
Oh, yeah. It's actually in my bedroom.

187
00:11:10,870 --> 00:11:12,250
That's right.

188
00:11:25,260 --> 00:11:26,890
What's up, Joey?

189
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:31,230
How you doing?

190
00:11:40,860 --> 00:11:43,360
- Excuse me. Is this your car?     - Yeah.

191
00:11:43,530 --> 00:11:46,740
Well, I don't think it's nice of you to park here. You're blocking the entrance.

192
00:11:46,990 --> 00:11:48,910
Don't worry about it. It's not a problem.

193
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:54,040
It's a problem for me, which means it's a problem for you because I'm a cop.

194
00:11:56,380 --> 00:11:57,750
So am I.

195
00:12:00,130 --> 00:12:01,760
Oh, no.

196
00:12:03,970 --> 00:12:07,050
Oh, okay. So you're a cop. You can park anywhere.

197
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:09,260
I know that because I'm a cop too.

198
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:12,020
All right. Keep up the good work. Ten-four.

199
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:14,890
Wait a second. So, what precinct are you with?

200
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:17,690
I'm with the, um, the 57th.

201
00:12:17,860 --> 00:12:21,190
- I know a guy in Homicide up there.     - I'm in Vice.

202
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:24,900
In fact, I'm undercover right now. I'm a whore.

203
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:29,030
Who else is in Vice up there?

204
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:30,990
Um, do you know, um...

205
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:32,500
...Sipowitz?

206
00:12:33,330 --> 00:12:35,330
Sipowitz? No, I don't think so.

207
00:12:35,540 --> 00:12:38,750
Yeah. Sipowitz. Yeah. Big guy, kind of bald.

208
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:40,960
I don't know him.

209
00:12:42,170 --> 00:12:45,470
Don't try to call him or anything. Because he's not there. He's out.

210
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:48,260
His, um, partner just died.

211
00:12:49,470 --> 00:12:52,310
Tell Sipowitz I'm real sorry for his loss.

212
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:54,930
I sure will. Take care.

213
00:12:55,140 --> 00:12:57,770
Hey, by the way, I'm sure Sipowitz is gonna be all right.

214
00:12:58,020 --> 00:13:00,980
I heard that kid from Silver Spoons is really good.

215
00:13:03,990 --> 00:13:05,740
Where'd you find my badge?

216
00:13:06,450 --> 00:13:07,490
Oh!

217
00:13:16,290 --> 00:13:20,340
Hey, Joey, would you mind giving me and Ross a hand moving his couch?

218
00:13:20,500 --> 00:13:23,460
Aw, I'd love to but I got acting class. But you know what?

219
00:13:23,670 --> 00:13:26,170
I guess I could blow that off for you.

220
00:13:31,010 --> 00:13:32,350
Thanks.

221
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:36,640
Uh, let me ask you something. I was talking with Monica and Chandler.

222
00:13:36,810 --> 00:13:38,690
Boy, they are really tight.

223
00:13:38,850 --> 00:13:39,900
I know.

224
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:42,190
That's not a bad situation they got over there.

225
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:43,900
Mm-mm.

226
00:13:44,440 --> 00:13:46,440
Thinking of getting me one of those.

227
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:51,370
What's up, Joe?

228
00:13:51,530 --> 00:13:54,910
The reason I think Monica and Chandler are so great...

229
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:57,750
...is because they were friends first, you know?

230
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:02,290
So I asked myself, who are my friends? You and Phoebe.

231
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:04,880
I saw you first, so...

232
00:14:06,550 --> 00:14:07,800
- Heh.     - Mm-hm.

233
00:14:07,970 --> 00:14:12,510
- What are you saying?     - I'm saying maybe you and I crank it up a notch.

234
00:14:16,350 --> 00:14:17,930
You know, honey, um...

235
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:20,480
...as, uh, flattered as I am...

236
00:14:20,730 --> 00:14:23,360
...that you saw me first...

237
00:14:24,150 --> 00:14:28,030
...uh, I just don't think we should be cranking anything up.

238
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:30,700
I'll treat you real nice.

239
00:14:36,290 --> 00:14:37,870
Oh!

240
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:40,620
Yeah. Well, you know, um...

241
00:14:41,580 --> 00:14:46,710
Listen, I think it's a great idea to become friends with someone before you date.

242
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:51,090
But I think the way you do it is you meet someone, become their friend...

243
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:54,760
...build a foundation, then ask them out on a date.

244
00:14:55,010 --> 00:14:57,520
Don't hit on your existing friends.

245
00:14:59,270 --> 00:15:01,940
Won't that take longer?

246
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:04,230
Yeah. Yeah.

247
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:06,320
Oh, but once you find it...

248
00:15:06,570 --> 00:15:08,740
...it's so worth the wait.

249
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:10,900
Yeah.

250
00:15:11,070 --> 00:15:12,160
I understand.

251
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:14,160
Good.

252
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:16,870
Man, I wish I saw Phoebe first.

253
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:21,710
Come here to me.

254
00:15:23,630 --> 00:15:25,920
No, no. You come here to me.

255
00:15:27,090 --> 00:15:29,300
Hey, Ross.

256
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:32,510
- Ahem, I brought reinforcements.     - Oh, great! You brought Joey?

257
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:34,220
I brought the next best thing. Heh.

258
00:15:34,390 --> 00:15:35,970
Hey.

259
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:40,520
You brought Chandler? The next best thing would be Monica!

260
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:45,520
I would be offended, but Monica is freakishly strong, so...

261
00:15:46,150 --> 00:15:48,610
Look, I drew a sketch of how we'll do it.

262
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:50,740
Rach, that's you.

263
00:15:50,950 --> 00:15:52,950
That's the couch.

264
00:15:53,110 --> 00:15:55,240
Oh, what's that?

265
00:15:55,490 --> 00:15:56,950
Oh, that's me.

266
00:15:58,040 --> 00:15:59,910
Wow.

267
00:16:01,330 --> 00:16:03,670
Certainly think a lot of yourself.

268
00:16:05,380 --> 00:16:07,290
No. That's my arm.

269
00:16:11,590 --> 00:16:15,760
Oh, I see. I thought you just really, really liked your new couch.

270
00:16:18,850 --> 00:16:20,640
Just follow my lead.

271
00:16:20,810 --> 00:16:22,480
Okay.

272
00:16:23,140 --> 00:16:24,940
Come on, Chandler.

273
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:26,270
Ah.

274
00:16:26,440 --> 00:16:27,770
- All right.     - Okay.

275
00:16:28,020 --> 00:16:30,230
Here we go.

276
00:16:30,400 --> 00:16:31,860
All right. Ready?

277
00:16:32,030 --> 00:16:33,190
- Yeah.     - Yeah.

278
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:34,450
- Turn!     - Okay.

279
00:16:34,610 --> 00:16:35,660
Turn!

280
00:16:35,820 --> 00:16:37,240
Turn!

281
00:16:37,910 --> 00:16:42,200
- I don't think we can turn anymore!     - I don't think it'll fit!

282
00:16:42,370 --> 00:16:45,370
Yeah, it will. Come on! Up, up, up!

283
00:16:45,540 --> 00:16:47,460
Up! Yes!

284
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:49,960
Here we go! Pivot!

285
00:16:50,670 --> 00:17:01,890
Pivot!

286
00:17:02,060 --> 00:17:05,180
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

287
00:17:09,110 --> 00:17:11,610
I don't think it's gonna pivot anymore.

288
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:13,150
You think?

289
00:17:15,490 --> 00:17:19,240
All right, let's, uh, bring it back down and try again.

290
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:21,620
Oh.

291
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:23,830
Whoa.

292
00:17:27,330 --> 00:17:29,880
I think it's really stuck now.

293
00:17:31,460 --> 00:17:35,010
- I can't believe that didn't work.     - I know. Me neither.

294
00:17:35,260 --> 00:17:36,970
I mean, you had a sketch.

295
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:41,470
What did you mean when you said "pivot"?

296
00:17:46,350 --> 00:17:47,390
- Hey.     - Hey.

297
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:50,190
How's it going? Did you make any new friends?

298
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:52,940
Yeah. I met this woman.

299
00:17:53,110 --> 00:17:54,900
Hey. Whoa, whoa.

300
00:17:55,070 --> 00:17:56,650
What's she like?

301
00:17:56,820 --> 00:17:58,530
Uh, well, she's...

302
00:17:58,700 --> 00:18:00,030
...really good in bed.

303
00:18:01,740 --> 00:18:03,790
I thought you were going to try to be friends first.

304
00:18:03,950 --> 00:18:07,120
- Hey, it's all your fault.     - What? Why?

305
00:18:07,290 --> 00:18:10,460
You didn't give me advice. You gave me a pickup line.

306
00:18:10,630 --> 00:18:14,460
I told her I wanted to "build a foundation and be friends."

307
00:18:14,630 --> 00:18:19,430
Suddenly, through no fault of my own, I became irresistible to her!

308
00:18:20,470 --> 00:18:21,800
And her roommate!

309
00:18:23,970 --> 00:18:25,720
What about the "closeness"?

310
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:30,440
Closeness, schmosness! There was three of us, for crying out loud!

311
00:18:35,110 --> 00:18:36,780
Who wants pizza?

312
00:18:36,940 --> 00:18:38,360
I do! I do! I do!

313
00:18:39,070 --> 00:18:42,950
This is great! Can you believe I found this on the second floor?

314
00:18:45,910 --> 00:18:47,910
- Who is it?     - NYPD.

315
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:50,160
- Oh, my God!     - Oh, my God.

316
00:18:50,540 --> 00:18:52,960
Uh, just a minute, officer!

317
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:06,310
- I'm looking for Phoebe Buffay.     - My God, it's him! It's that cop!

318
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:10,520
- I can't believe he found me!     - Are you going to go to jail?

319
00:19:10,980 --> 00:19:13,900
If I'm going down, you guys are going down with me.

320
00:19:15,820 --> 00:19:19,440
Harboring a fugitive? That's one-to-three years minimum.

321
00:19:19,820 --> 00:19:21,740
Good luck, Chandler.

322
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:29,200
You can arrest me, but you'll never make it stick and you know it.

323
00:19:29,370 --> 00:19:32,750
I kind of don't have a choice, it's my job. You understand, right?

324
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:35,710
Yeah, as long as you understand that I'm gonna call my lawyer.

325
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:39,800
And once he puts you on the stand, he's gonna make you look like a fool! Like a fool!

326
00:19:41,630 --> 00:19:43,590
I don't like looking foolish.

327
00:19:44,050 --> 00:19:48,220
Maybe, uh, I don't arrest you today. Maybe I came by and you weren't here.

328
00:19:48,390 --> 00:19:50,600
I would love it if I weren't here!

329
00:19:51,310 --> 00:19:55,350
Since, um, you're not going to jail tonight, I was wondering if you'd, um...

330
00:19:55,610 --> 00:19:57,820
...like to go to dinner with me?

331
00:19:58,530 --> 00:19:59,780
- Me?     - Yeah.

332
00:19:59,940 --> 00:20:03,780
Ever since you flashed my badge at me, I kind of can't stop thinking about you.

333
00:20:04,030 --> 00:20:07,830
You're the prettiest fake undercover whore I've ever seen.

334
00:20:09,450 --> 00:20:11,410
Nice.

335
00:20:13,460 --> 00:20:16,920
Wow, I didn't see that coming. You're asking me out.

336
00:20:17,130 --> 00:20:20,550
Yeah, I could've done it better, but these people keep staring at me.

337
00:20:20,710 --> 00:20:24,970
Um, yeah, I'd like to go out with you, officer.

338
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:27,600
- Gary.     - Gary.

339
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:29,760
- Okay, so it's a date.     - Yeah.

340
00:20:29,930 --> 00:20:32,560
I gotta ask you, though. How did you know where to find me?

341
00:20:32,810 --> 00:20:35,900
Your fingerprints were all over my badge so I ran them through the computer.

342
00:20:36,060 --> 00:20:38,770
This was listed as your last known address so I checked it out.

343
00:20:38,940 --> 00:20:39,980
Oh, impressive.

344
00:20:40,150 --> 00:20:44,530
Not as impressive as you. I looked at your record and you've done some weird stuff.

345
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:46,410
We'll talk at dinner.

346
00:20:46,570 --> 00:20:47,820
Okay.

347
00:20:47,990 --> 00:20:50,030
So I'll come by in a couple hours and pick you up?

348
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:51,700
- All right, I can't wait.     - Okay.

349
00:20:51,870 --> 00:20:54,710
Don't worry, I won't just take you out for doughnuts.

350
00:20:58,090 --> 00:20:59,500
He has a gun!

351
00:21:06,010 --> 00:21:09,640
I'd like to return this couch. I'm not satisfied with it.

352
00:21:14,520 --> 00:21:17,060
You want to return this couch?

353
00:21:18,520 --> 00:21:21,190
It's cut in half.

354
00:21:22,070 --> 00:21:26,320
- That's what I'm telling you.     - Did you cut this couch in half?

355
00:21:27,740 --> 00:21:30,780
This couch is cut in half!

356
00:21:32,240 --> 00:21:37,290
I would like to exchange it for one that is not cut in half.

357
00:21:37,540 --> 00:21:41,040
You're telling me this couch was delivered to you like this?

358
00:21:41,210 --> 00:21:43,420
Look, I'm a reasonable man.

359
00:21:43,590 --> 00:21:46,670
I will accept store credit.

360
00:21:47,380 --> 00:21:51,390
I'll give you store credit in the amount of $4.

361
00:21:54,850 --> 00:21:56,520
I will take it.

